title: StartScreen
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: This place is kind of... bland?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Bland is fine. It's better than <i>roaches</i>.
===

title: Intro
---
<<declare $DrainCount = 0>>

<<declare $KeyTrigger = false>>

<<SetIntro DialogueManager>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
<i>Maya's phone rings.</i>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Edgar: Hey, Noah and Maya! Get into the house okay?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Maya: Edgar, usually the landlord shows up for the start of a tour-

<<CallVO DialogueManager 3>>
Edgar: Just finishing up some renovations at another property, be there soon.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 4>>
Noah: Oh, we can wait outside.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 5>>
<i>The door jiggles but doesn't budge.</i>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 6>>
Maya: Is the door locked?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 7>>
Edgar: It does that. Just find the key.
===


title: HalfKeyTip
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Well, there’s half of the key. 

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Edgar: Yeah, the previous tenants broke a lot of stuff.  

===

title: KeyFlyer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Why do landlords always use the weirdest locks and keys imaginable?
===
title: KeyFlyer2
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Why do landlords always use the weirdest locks and keys imaginable?
===

title: DoorLook
---

<<if $KeyTrigger == true>>
    <<stop>>    
<<endif>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: There’s the symbol of a key on the door...
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Must be a reminder. Like, “in case you lose it, here’s what the key looks like!”
<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Maya: I guess that’s necessary if your front door randomly <i>locks you inside</i>.
===

title: KeySolve
---
<<wait 11>>
<<set $KeyTrigger = true>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Didn't that door lead outside before?

<<SetKey DialogueManager>>
===

title: StairLook
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Does that staircase just... go nowhere?
===

title: LoftEnter
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: What the...

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: It's like we're in an Escher drawing.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Edgar: Do you like the mood lighting?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 3>>
Maya: Edgar, how do we get out? It’s so dark in here.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 4>>
Edgar: Just turn on the lamp.

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 120 LampTimer LampSolve>>
===


title: HalfHintLamp
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: That looks like half of a lamp.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: The lamp's broken, too? How much do we need to fix before we get out of here?
===

title: HalfHintPineapple
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Is this pineapple... radioactive? 
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: Why's it glowing?
===
title: HalfHintPineapple2
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Is this pineapple... radioactive?
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Why's it glowing?
===

title: HalfHintKnob
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Aww, is that a little wooden train set?
===
title: HalfHintTrophy
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Is that bear made of wood? Not exactly huggable.
===

title: HalfHintPlunger2
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Is that a gramophone? How old is Edgar?
===
title: HalfHintPlunger
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Is that a gramophone? How old is Edgar?
===
title: HalfHintHandle
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Why are these curtains... hanging... up?
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: I wish Edgar would hang up.
<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Edgar: I got the highest quality curtain rods money can buy!
===

title: HalfHintDrain
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: How does a shower work in Escher gravity?
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Please don't make me think about it.
===
title: HalfHintLotus
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: I think we've found the source of the flood.
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Lotuses. Prettiest toilet clog I've ever seen.
<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Maya: And you've seen a lot of them.
<<CallVO DialogueManager 3>>
Noah: Hey.
===

title: HalfHintExtinguisher
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Edgar's taste in sculpture is, um. Avant-garde.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: I wonder if it's one of those magic-eye things that makes a shape.
===
title: HalfHintMobile
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Love all the... <i>modern</i> art.
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Blood red is an interesting color choice. Sorta looks like an eldritch baby mobile. 
===

title: HalfHintExit
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Not gonna ask why there’s a broken exit sign in a closet.
===
title: HalfHintExit2
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Not gonna ask why there’s a broken exit sign in a closet.
===


title: LampTimer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: I bet the lamp’s broken, too.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: What here looks like half a lamp?
===

title: LampSolve
---
<<wait 4>>
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Why do I not see a way outside?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: At least we can see.

<<StartDialogue DialogueManager LivingRoomEnter>>
===


title: LivingRoomEnter
---

<<wait 0.5>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Edgar: Beautiful, right? The living room is open-concept. This one-of-a-kind space has a built in fireplace AND water feature.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: I knew DIY renovation could get bad, but-

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Noah: No wonder this place was in our price range. There must be an exit in here...

<<wait 4>>  
<<CallVO DialogueManager 3>>
Noah: Am I the only one who finds it odd that we just fixed a lamp by attaching it to a similar-looking pineapple?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 4>>
Maya: One thing at a time. Let's look for a way out.
===

title: FireLook
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Edgar: Note the classy built-in fireplace.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: Edgar. The house is just on fire.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Noah: Let’s find an extinguisher before we die, maybe? Although I wouldn’t count on this guy installing one.

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 120 ExtinguisherTimer ExtinguisherSolve>>
===

title: ClogLook
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Ugh, god. What's clogging that pipe?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Edgar: I think I left the plunger... upstairs? No, maybe by the record player.

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 120 PlungerTimer PlungerSolve>>
===

title: ExtinguisherTimer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: You'd think a bright red extinguisher would be easy to find.
===

title: PlungerTimer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Edgar said to check upstairs and by the record player for the plunger.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: What shapes make a plunger? Something round for the cup, and a rod for the handle?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
<i>Noah giggles.</i>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 3>>
Maya: What, cups and rods are making you laugh? Shut up.
===

title: PlungerFlyer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: That's always a good message to get from a plumber.
===
title: PlungerFlyer2
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: That's always a good message to get from a plumber.
===

title: GeneralFlyer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Please tell me it says something nice this time.
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: What do <i>you</i> think?
===

title: HalfUnsolvable
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Have you seen the other half of this?
<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: No. Maybe it's in a room we haven't seen yet.
===

title: ExtinguisherSolve
---
<<SetExtinguisher DialogueManager>>

<<wait 10>>  

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Our chances of dying have lowered! Slightly.
===

title: PlungerSolve
---
<<SetPlunger DialogueManager>>

<<wait 10>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Glad the clog's gone. That was grossing me out.
===

title: Unsolvable
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: I don’t think I’ve seen the pieces to solve this yet. 

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Maybe we should find a way into the rooms that are still inaccessible.
===

title: ClosetLook
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Edgar, did you just... not finish this wall?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Edgar: I always lose a piece from jigsaw puzzles. I might've left it in the bedroom?

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 120 DoorknobTimer DoorKnobSolve>>
===
title: ClosetLook2
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Edgar, did you just... not finish this wall?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Edgar: I always lose a piece from jigsaw puzzles. I might've left it in the bedroom?

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 120 DoorknobTimer DoorKnobSolve>>
===

title: WaterfallLook
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Do you see something behind all that water? Maybe it’s an exit.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: If we could just drain it- looks like a bathroom pipe burst. Yuck.
===


title: BedroomEntrance
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Don’t you just hate falling out of bed in the morning?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: No exit here. Maybe more of Edgar’s broken stuff to fix, though.
===

title: DoorknobTimer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: We're looking for a puzzle piece, right?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Let's check the bedroom for parts that could fit that shape.
===

title: TenantFlyer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: This must’ve been left by the last people who lived here.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: Willing to bet he forced them out just to flip the house. Literally, I guess.
===


title: BathroomEnter
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Edgar: As you can see, the bathroom has a lovely walk-in jacuzzi.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: It's flooded! And everything's... giant?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Edgar: As I said, walk-in. Just use the drain if there's too much water.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 3>>
Maya: His lease definitely has a mold disclosure.

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 120 DrainTimer DrainSolve>>
===

title: DrainTimer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: We have to get rid of the flood.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Maya: Half of a drain would just be a semicircle full of holes, right?

===

title: DrainSolve
---
<<wait 20>>

<<wait 20>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: So, that opens to... a broken exit sign. That feels cruel.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: We'll find a way out of here somehow.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Edgar: Exits are clearly labeled!
===

title: DoorKnobSolve
---
<<wait 0.5>>

<<SetDrain DialogueManager>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Edgar. We've gone through every door. Where is the exit?

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Edgar: The sign should be obvious.

<<DialogueDelay DialogueManager 180 ExitTimer ExitSolve>>
===

title: DoorDrainSwitch
---
<<if $DrainCount == 0>>
    <<set $DrainCount to 1>>
    <<StartDialogue DialogueManager DrainSolve>>
<<elseif $DrainCount > 0>>
    <<StartDialogue DialogueManager DoorKnobSolve>>
<<endif>>
===

title: ExitTimer
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Noah: Maybe fixing an exit sign could help us get out of here. Would fit this place’s logic.
===

title: ExitSolve
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
Maya: Finally. A way out.

<<CallVO DialogueManager 1>>
Noah: Thank god we escaped.

<<wait 4>>

<<CallVO DialogueManager 2>>
Edgar: So. Do you want to rent the house?
===

title: CreditsScreen
---
<<CallVO DialogueManager 0>>
<i>Edgar rambles about the house over the phone. He should wear himself out, eventually.</i>
===